<h2>Level 4 · Linking by relationship (knowledge graph)</h2>
<p>Where Level 3 found <strong>"things close in meaning,"</strong> Level 4 follows <strong>"what is tied to what, and how."</strong> That is the <strong>knowledge graph</strong>. The question takes the shape <strong>"start at X and trace the connections through to A."</strong> It is usually the <strong>most powerful but also the most complex and costly</strong> stage.</p>

<h3>Entities + relationships = a graph</h3>
<p>A knowledge graph is made of two things: <strong>entities (people, companies, products)</strong> and the <strong>named relationships between them (who works where, what endorses what)</strong>. Unlike wiki links, the <strong>relationship carries meaning (a type)</strong>.</p>

