<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">It can be lighter than a wiki</span>
    A wiki makes you <strong>read related pages in full</strong> (as in "reading the entire AI video production document when all you need is 11Labs"). A graph only needs you to touch <strong>the edges (relationships) you need</strong>, so in such cases it is <strong>actually lighter.</strong>
</div>

<h3>Tools — LightRAG · Graphiti · GraphRAG</h3>
<p>Usually <strong>software extracts the entities and relationships automatically</strong> and builds the graph for you. The notable ones:</p>
