<p>So before blaming the system, ask yourself first: <strong>"Are my folders really as <em>holistic</em> as what is in my head?"</strong> The habit of feeding in materials, contracts, and subtitles while fleshing them out through <strong>brainstorming</strong> is the key.</p>

<div class="note warn">
    <span class="nh">Privacy — where is the data going</span>
    Processing your data with a Claude model means the content is <strong>sent to Anthropic</strong>. That may be acceptable for your own work materials, but it is a different story for <strong>customer data or sensitive information</strong>. In those cases consider running <strong>open-source or local models</strong> and keeping the Second Brain that holds everything <strong>local rather than in the cloud</strong>. Being <strong>aware yourself</strong> of what gets processed where comes first.
</div>

